  "limits": [
    "Whole-value xattrs are bounded to 262143 bytes within one existing immutable object. No inode/manifest format change. Existing values <=64 KiB need no rewrite; older daemons/frontends reject larger values.",
    "The tested native macOS 27.2 path rejected exactly 262144 bytes with EFBIG even when the callback allowed it. The shared bound excludes that endpoint. Inode RPC and direct callback oversize rejection is E2BIG.",
    "ResourceFork whole-value get/set works, but cp -p and position reads return EINVAL on forkfs; APFS completes both. This is not full resource-fork stream/copy compatibility.",
    "Ordinary large xattrs survive cp -p. The retained copy inode receives its resource fork through a separate whole-value set, not a successful resource-fork copy.",
    "The 32-attribute count limit remains. No arbitrary-size/chunked xattrs, quotas, named-fork stream or full POSIX/APFS compatibility claim."
  ]
